WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.220
At Cape Canaveral, Florida, the Army's Jupiter-C rocket is ready for America's second attempt

00:10.220 --> 00:12.100
to launch a space satellite.

00:12.100 --> 00:17.900
No relation to the IRBM Jupiter, this is a rebuilt Redstone, a 200-mile missile carrying

00:17.900 --> 00:23.940
instead of a warhead three stages of solid fuel booster rockets and the Explorer, a six-foot

00:23.940 --> 00:38.040
bullet only inches across crammed with electronic gear, 30 pounds of payload.

00:38.040 --> 00:41.680
This close-up of the United States edition of Sputnik was made at a press conference

00:41.680 --> 00:46.800
with leaders of the scientific teams, Dr. Werner von Braun, Dr. James Van Allen and Dr.

00:46.800 --> 00:51.680
William Pickering, a three-way collaboration between private industry, academic science

00:51.680 --> 00:55.000
and the military.

00:55.000 --> 00:57.360
The university stands poised on its launching pad.

00:57.360 --> 00:59.640
The hours-long countdown approaches zero.

00:59.640 --> 01:03.920
A moment of enormous tension for every missile launching is still an experiment.

01:03.920 --> 01:08.360
Any one of tens of thousands of things can go wrong with catastrophic results, but all

01:08.360 --> 01:10.480
that can be done to assure perfection has been done.

01:10.480 --> 01:11.480
The moment is at hand.

01:11.480 --> 01:25.880
The countdown reaches zero.

01:25.880 --> 01:31.040
Some three minutes later, Explorer is in orbit, broadcasting to the world its coded scientific

01:31.040 --> 01:32.040
data.

01:32.040 --> 01:38.080
Cosmic ray intensity, meteor impact, solar radiation, these are the dry facts that will

01:38.080 --> 01:49.440
help carry man ever farther into the age of space.

01:49.440 --> 01:54.560
Two presidents, Kamal Abdel Nasser of Egypt and Shukri al-Khawatli of Syria meet to make

01:54.560 --> 02:00.680
history in Cairo with the federation of their two states into one, the United Arab Republic.

02:00.680 --> 02:08.320
The news electrified the entire Middle East, in Cairo, cheering throngs followed the two

02:08.320 --> 02:16.120
leaders through the streets exultantly.

02:16.120 --> 02:20.560
The Al-Haza Mosque is the scene of prayers for the new union, which has already invited

02:20.560 --> 02:22.360
all Arab states to join.

02:22.360 --> 02:25.360
One, Yemen, is expected to bid for inclusion.

02:25.360 --> 02:28.560
The new state number is 30 million, largest in the Mideast.

02:28.560 --> 02:31.400
Syria sent vast forces in motion with this act.

02:31.400 --> 02:36.000
The effect on the precariously balanced Middle East, no one today can prophesy.

02:36.000 --> 02:41.600
The rest of the world, America, Russia, Israel, all remain cautiously quiet awaiting the events

02:41.600 --> 03:00.760
that will follow on Kamal Nasser's moment of triumph.

